From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode <opencode@localhost>
Date: Fri, 02 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Bugfix] Stop mamba align prefill at the replay boundary
 (upstream #50409)

Version-locked to VLLM_REF=v0.31.0 (rebased; the final grew Marconi
junction stops and a conditional tail_boundary entry since rc3 - pure
context shift, pre-image blob unchanged. Logic identical to upstream:
compute replay_boundary, add it as a mandatory chunk stop).
Upstream PR #50409 (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/50409)
still open, in no tag. Drop when VLLM_REF contains the fix.
Rebased 2026-10-09 onto the PRISTINE v0.31.0 tag when the 40707
deadlock patch was dropped: hunk 1's old context line was the
20-space-indented `end = aligned_end` inside the 40707 patch's else
branch, so the patch hard-depended on 40707 being applied first. The
context line is now pristine's 16-space `end = aligned_end` and the
hunks shifted -11 lines (491->480, 524->513); final-state identity with
the old ordered apply was verified by full-tree diff.

When the prompt length is an exact multiple of the scheduler block
size, align prefill runs as one chunk and the only cached Mamba state
sits at num_tokens, which get_computed_blocks caps below - the Mamba
group then reports a 0-token hit and the reconciled hybrid hit is 0.
Adding the replay boundary (min((num_tokens-1)//block_size*block_size,
last_cache_position)) as a mandatory chunk stop materializes a state a
later replay can resume from.
---
diff --git a/vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py b/vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
index 8b188de..a81364a 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
@@ -480,6 +480,16 @@ class Scheduler(SchedulerInterface):
                 end = aligned_end
 
         next_block_boundary = (start // block_size + 1) * block_size
+        # A later request replaying this prompt resumes at `num_tokens - 1`
+        # at the latest (`get_computed_blocks` caps the hit there), so the
+        # block boundary at or below that must be a chunk end too: when
+        # `num_tokens` is an exact multiple of `block_size` the only state
+        # cached below it would otherwise sit one token above the cap,
+        # missing entirely (upstream #50409).
+        replay_boundary = min(
+            (request.num_tokens - 1) // block_size * block_size,
+            last_cache_position,
+        )
         tail_boundary = (
             request.num_prompt_tokens // self.hash_block_size * self.hash_block_size
             if self.mamba_partial_cache_hit and not use_internal_checkpoint
@@ -513,6 +523,9 @@ class Scheduler(SchedulerInterface):
             else 0,
             # Never run past the last cacheable block boundary mid-chunk.
             last_cache_position,
+            # Keep the boundary a replay of this prompt can resume from
+            # (exact-multiple-of-block-size prefill; upstream #50409).
+            replay_boundary if start < replay_boundary < end else 0,
             # Fine-grained hits: the prompt's partial-tail entry can only be
             # registered by a chunk ending exactly at its last hash boundary.
             tail_boundary
